her family for over 20 years. These cookies were enjoyed by her children Sarah, Melanie, and Nicholas as well as her husband Paul. Friends and family also enjoyed these cookies and looked forward to them whenever they had a chance to imbibe.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]], softened\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:White Sugar|white sugar]]\n* ¼ cup packed [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]]\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Vanilla|vanilla]]\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] salt\n* ½ tsp [[Cookbook:Baking Soda|baking soda]]\n* Hershey's Chipits semisweet [[Cookbook:Chocolate Chip|chocolate chips]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n# [[Cookbook:Creaming|Cream]] butter and sugar in a bowl until well combined.\n# Mix in egg and vanilla.\n# Combine flour, salt, and baking soda. Mix this dry mix into the wet mix.\n# [[Cookbook:Folding|Fold]] in chocolate chips.\n# Scoop cookies onto a [[Cookbook:Parchment Paper|parchment]]-lined [[Cookbook:Baking Sheet|baking sheet]]. [[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] at 350°F until golden brown.\n# Cool slightly, then remove from baking sheet. Cool fully.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using dark chocolate]]\n[[Category:Recipes for chocolate chip cookies]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking soda]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using white sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Chocolate Chip Cookies III","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"½ cup butter, softened","sourceText":"½ cup butter, softened","amountText":"½ cup butter, softened","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"½ cup white sugar","sourceText":"½ cup white sugar","amountText":"½ cup white sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3"